 "speed": 0.88,
 "text": "Chatbots like ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini all run on one idea: the transformer. Its job sounds simple. Guess the next word. First, your text is cut into small pieces, and each piece becomes a list of numbers that stands for its meaning. Words that mean similar things get similar numbers. Then comes the clever part: attention. Every word looks at every other word, to work out what it means here. In the sentence, the cat sat because it was tired, the word it looks hardest at cat. Older models read one word at a time, and forgot the start. A transformer reads all the words at once, so it can learn from huge amounts of text, fast. This step is repeated in many layers. Early layers notice grammar. Later layers pick up meaning and facts. At the end, it scores every possible next word, picks a likely one, adds it, and starts again. Word by word, that's how it writes.",
